#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:1
msgid "Launch Gazebo from ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:3
msgid "Gazebo can be launched from a ROS 2 launch system in multiple ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:5
msgid "Using the launch files included in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:6
msgid ""
"[ros_gz_sim](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/tree/jazzy/ros_gz_sim)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:8
msgid ""
"The package `ros_gz_sim` contains two launch files named `gz_server.launch."
"py` and `gz_sim.launch.py`. You can use them to start Gazebo server or "
"Gazebo (server and GUI) respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:12
msgid "ros2 launch ros_gz_sim gz_sim.launch.py gz_args:=empty.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:16
msgid "Or you can just start the server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:18
msgid "ros2 launch ros_gz_sim gz_server.launch.py world_sdf_file:=empty.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:22
msgid ""
"Consult the argument block of each launch file [here](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/gz_sim.launch.py.in#L75-L96) "
"and [here](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/"
"gz_server.launch.py#L27-L38) to learn about the different parameters that "
"are accepted by each launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:27
msgid "Using a custom launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:29
msgid "XML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:30
msgid ""
"It's also possible to start Gazebo from your custom launch file. For that "
"purpose we have created the custom `<gz_server/>` tag that can be used from "
"your XML launch file. In this case, the arguments are passed as attributes "
"within this tag. Here's an example for launching Gazebo server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:35
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <arg name=\"world_sdf_file\" default=\"empty.sdf\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"world_sdf_string\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"container_name\" default=\"ros_gz_container\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"create_own_container\" default=\"False\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"use_composition\" default=\"False\" />\n"
"  <gz_server\n"
"    world_sdf_file=\"$(var world_sdf_file)\"\n"
"    world_sdf_string=\"$(var world_sdf_string)\"\n"
"    container_name=\"$(var container_name)\"\n"
"    create_own_container=\"$(var create_own_container)\"\n"
"    use_composition=\"$(var use_composition)\">\n"
"  </gz_server>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:52
msgid ""
"In this case the `<gz_server>` parameters are read from the command line. "
"That's an option but not strictly necessary as you could decide to hardcode "
"some of the values or not even use all the parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:56
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:57
msgid ""
"Python launch files provide more low-level customization and logic compared "
"to XML launch files. For example, you can set environment variables and "
"include Python specific functions and logic. In the following example, the "
"user can replace the example package, world, and bridged topic with their "
"own. This is intended as a scaffolding more than something that can be run "
"on its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:60
msgid ""
"from ament_index_python.packages import get_package_share_directory\n"
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch_ros.actions import Node\n"
"from launch.actions import SetEnvironmentVariable, IncludeLaunchDescription\n"
"from launch.launch_description_sources import PythonLaunchDescriptionSource\n"
"from launch.substitutions import PathJoinSubstitution\n"
"from launch_ros.substitutions import FindPackageShare\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    ros_gz_sim_pkg_path = get_package_share_directory('ros_gz_sim')\n"
"    example_pkg_path = FindPackageShare('example_package')  # Replace with "
"your own package name\n"
"    gz_launch_path = PathJoinSubstitution([ros_gz_sim_pkg_path, 'launch', "
"'gz_sim.launch.py'])\n"
"\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        SetEnvironmentVariable(\n"
"            'GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH',\n"
"            PathJoinSubstitution([example_pkg_path, 'models'])\n"
"        ),\n"
"        SetEnvironmentVariable(\n"
"            'GZ_SIM_PLUGIN_PATH',\n"
"            PathJoinSubstitution([example_pkg_path, 'plugins'])\n"
"        ),\n"
"        IncludeLaunchDescription(\n"
"            PythonLaunchDescriptionSource(gz_launch_path),\n"
"            launch_arguments={\n"
"                'gz_args': [PathJoinSubstitution([example_pkg_path, 'worlds/"
"example_world.sdf'])],  # Replace with your own world file\n"
"                'on_exit_shutdown': 'True'\n"
"            }.items(),\n"
"        ),\n"
"\n"
"        # Bridging and remapping Gazebo topics to ROS 2 (replace with your "
"own topics)\n"
"        Node(\n"
"            package='ros_gz_bridge',\n"
"            executable='parameter_bridge',\n"
"            arguments=['/example_imu_topic@sensor_msgs/msg/Imu@gz.msgs."
"IMU',],\n"
"            remappings=[('/example_imu_topic',\n"
"                         '/remapped_imu_topic'),],\n"
"            output='screen'\n"
"        ),\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:104
msgid ""
"Here's another example using a higher level action from Python to launch "
"`gzserver`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:105
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch.actions import DeclareLaunchArgument\n"
"from launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration\n"
"from ros_gz_sim.actions import GzServer\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"\n"
"    declare_world_sdf_file_cmd = DeclareLaunchArgument(\n"
"        'world_sdf_file', default_value='',\n"
"        description='Path to the SDF world file')\n"
"\n"
"    # Create the launch description and populate\n"
"    ld = LaunchDescription([\n"
"        GzServer(\n"
"            world_sdf_file=LaunchConfiguration('world_sdf_file')\n"
"        ),\n"
"    ])\n"
"\n"
"    # Declare the launch options\n"
"    ld.add_action(declare_world_sdf_file_cmd)\n"
"\n"
"    return ld\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:132
msgid "Launching with ros_gz_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:134
msgid ""
"An example launch file for XML can be viewed [here](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/ros_gz_sim.launch) An example "
"launch file for Python can be viewed [here](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/ros_gz_sim.launch.py)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:137
msgid ""
"Example command for directly using these launch files from the terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:138
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_sim ros_gz_sim.launch.py world_sdf_file:=empty.sdf "
"bridge_name:=ros_gz_bridge config_file:=<path_to_your_YAML_file> "
"use_composition:=True create_own_container:=True\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:142
msgid ""
"In the above launch files you may notice that the `create_own_container` "
"argument for `ros_gz_bridge` is hardcoded to `False`. This has been done to "
"prevent two duplicate containers from getting created (one for `gz_server` "
"and another one for `ros_gz_bridge`), and instead make `ros_gz_bridge` use "
"the container created by `gz_server`. More info about this can be viewed "
"[here](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/pull/620#issue-2595570189)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:144
msgid ""
"More info about `ros_gz_bridge` can be viewed [here](ros2_integration). More "
"info about composition can be viewed [here](ros2_overview.md#composition)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:147
msgid "Further Considerations for ROS2 Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:149
msgid ""
"If you're planning to use `ros2_control` with Gazebo, please take a look at "
"the [example launch files](https://github.com/ros-controls/gz_ros2_control/"
"tree/rolling/gz_ros2_control_demos/launch) in the `gz_ros2_control` "
"repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:151
msgid ""
"It is essential to publish the `/clock` topic for the `controller_manager` "
"to function correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:153
msgid ""
" gz_bridge = Node(\n"
"     package=\"ros_gz_bridge\",\n"
"     executable=\"parameter_bridge\",\n"
"     arguments=['/clock@rosgraph_msgs/msg/Clock[gz.msgs.Clock'],\n"
"     parameters=[{\n"
"         \"qos_overrides./tf_static.publisher.durability\": "
"\"transient_local\"\n"
"     }],\n"
"     output=\"screen\",\n"
" )\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:163
msgid ""
"If you **do not** publish the `/clock` topic, the `controller_manager` will "
"issue warnings or errors such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:165
msgid ""
"   [gazebo-1] [WARN] [1744219953.983130822] [controller_manager]: No clock "
"received, using time argument instead! Check your node's clock configuration "
"(use_sim_time parameter) and if a valid clock source is available.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:167
msgid "Timing Issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:170
msgid ""
"By default, the `controller_manager` launched by `gz_ros2_control` has "
"``use_sim_time=true``. If for any reason this is set to ``false``, it will "
"fall back to the system clock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:172
msgid "This results in logs like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:174
msgid ""
" [gazebo-1] [INFO] [1744209678.974210234] [gz_ros_control]: Loading "
"controller_manager\n"
" [gazebo-1] [INFO] [1744209679.000651931] [controller_manager]: Using Steady "
"(Monotonic) clock for triggering controller manager cycles.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:177
msgid "Eventually leading to a fatal error:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:179
msgid ""
" [gazebo-1] terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::"
"runtime_error'\n"
" [gazebo-1]   what():  can't compare times with different time sources\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_launch_gazebo.md:182
msgid ""
"Ensure `use_sim_time` is correctly set to `true` when working with "
"simulation time to avoid such mismatches."
msgstr ""
